# narrative-deck — working rules

## Never modify
- Anything inside `docs/` once moved there. The code is tested.
- No refactoring, no "improvements", no reformatting.

## Never add
- Dependencies, package.json, build steps, bundlers, frameworks.
- This project is vanilla HTML/CSS/JS by design.

## Word limits — hard
- SKILL.md: under 500 words
- Each reference file: under 400 words
- Exceeding these makes the skill load unreliably.

## Two purposes, kept separate
- `docs/` teaches humans what effects exist and why they hook.
- `skill/` specifies for agents how to build them.
- Do not duplicate prose between them.

